'''Baki Hanma''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Baki Hanma Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 789
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Baki Hanma
|name2 = Baki Hanma CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Baki Hanma CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
An interesting unit with a bizarre set of abilities, Baki functions as an [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] crowd-controller with a 30% chance of [[Shield Piercing]] and a 75% chance to [[Knockback]] Aku enemies. In this respect, he operates similarly to [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]], but with a far higher attack rate and no [[Long Distance]] attacks. However, he lacks immunity to [[Surge Attack|Surges]] and has an abysmal health pool; the immunities he does have are irrelevant against Aku, [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]]. While his other abilities are questionable, they do improve his generalist usage—although his [[Critical Hit]] chance is still too low to be used optimally on Metals.

All in all, Baki is not well-suited to tackle and grapple with Aku enemies. While his generalist damage is quite good, especially at 450 range and with such a short cooldown, it faces heavy competition in lategame from the likes of [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Minka]], with their ability to [[Weaken]] all enemies. Even with his high range he is extraordinarily fragile, vulnerable to enemies that even lightly graze him, which makes him risky to use against Zombies.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner & Crowd-Controller}}

